Meta <a href="https://x.com/instagram/status/2125295853816692960">today expanded</a> what Muse can do in Instagram, making the personal AI agent more useful.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/muse-instagram.jpg" alt="" width="1671" height="940" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079388" /><br/>
Muse can organize the Instagram content you save into collections or travel itineraries, plus it can make grocery lists for recipes you find. Meta says you can also chat with Muse in DMs to learn more about a post or catch up on what you've missed.<br/>
<br/>
When saving a post on Instagram, users in the U.S. and Canada will see an option to have Muse organize their posts. Muse in DMs will show up as a standard conversation.<br/>
<br/>
As <em><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/24/meta-brings-its-muse-ai-assistant-directly-into-instagram-dms/">TechCrunch</a></em> points out, Muse for Instagram DMs lets users chat with the AI agent without having to switch from Instagram to the Muse app and back again. Conversations with Muse on Instagram will also appear as a side chat in the Muse app.<br/>
<br/>
